    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;Kotaiyin katal&quot; is a historical fiction set 1200 years ago, reimagined by the creative genius Kanyudraj. The story follows the life of Andal, who carries the beloved memories of Andal with her every day. During a pilgrimage to the Thiruvilliputhur temple, Andal finds herself caught in a mysterious situation. Kanyudraj&apos;s narrative unfolds as Andal is held at the banks of the Kaveri River, while the pilgrims from Mettukudi engage in a dialogue that leads her to a profound decision. As the river flows, Andal is engulfed by it, leading to a poignant and transformative conclusion.</marc:subfield>
